@base <http://ecareathome-ontology.mpi.aass.oru.se/patterns/SmartHome_FeatureOfInterest.owl> .

<http://ecareathome-ontology.mpi.aass.oru.se/patterns/SmartHome_FeatureOfInterest.owl> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                                                        owl:imports <http://ecareathome-ontology.mpi.aass.oru.se/patterns/SmartHome_Property.owl> ;
                                                                                        dcterms:description "Diagram | Competency Questions: | ..."^^xsd:string ;
                                                                                        dcterms:title "Smarthome Featureofinterest Pattern"^^xsd:string ;
                                                                                        cpannotationschema:coversRequirements "What is the object which is the interest of the observation process? Which property pf this object is important?"^^xsd:string ,
                                                                                                                              "Which sensing process (SSN:Sensing) is monitoring the state of the feature of interest (i.e. a specific property of the object)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                                                        cpannotationschema:isSpecializationOf "This pattern extends the DUL ontology. The extension is in the form of specialization of the following classes: DUL:InformationObject. According to DULCE an information object is defined as a piece of information independently from how it is concretely realized. There are many situations where a feature of interest is seen as merely a piece of information without mentioning its numerical (e.g. 70 degree) or even symbolic (e.g. warm) values. We therefore specialize the class DUL:InformationObject so as to represent the class SmartHomeFeatureOfInterest whose instances will be as pieces of information objects allocated with numeric values during an observation process."^^xsd:string ;
                                                                                        cpannotationschema:scenarios "A feature of interest can be \"the pressure sensed on the couch\" or \"the electric-current of the TV\"."^^xsd:string ;
                                                                                        rdfs:comment """Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK's quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x12; term declared x6;
- header: dcterms:title \"Smarthome Featureofinterest Pattern\" - the library's name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library's description of the pattern
Each change is listed under \"curated\" in the pattern's metadata.json in OntoBoard's pattern library."""@en .

